Switch settings are for monitor values. Switch 1 is the closest to the
stereo connector (the little round one).

Switch Setting    Pixel Freq(Mhz)    Resolution        Refresh Rate(Hz)
dddd                    130                     1280x1024            72
uddd                    119                        1280x1024        66
dudd                    108                    1280x1024            60
uudd                    104                    1152x900            72
ddud                    93                        1152x900            66
udud                    75                        1024x768            70
duud                    74                        1024x768            72
uuud                    69                        1024x864            60
dddu                    65                        1024x768            60
uddu                    50                        800x600                72
dudu                    40                        800x600                60
uudu                    32                        640x480                72
dduu                    25                        640x480                60
uduu                    135                        1280x1024            75
duuu                    110                        1280x1024            60
uuuu                    reserved

Switch settings are up down; up is toward the side of the board with the
chips on it. I believe modes 13 and 14 are stereo modes. Hope this helps.

Dave
