I don't know about TurboLinux (if they sell Alpha versions) RedHat does
(wich is'nt to good though) I suggest a SuSE AXP version.
It comes with Beowulf (wich is a performance cluster software).
You might want to concider that caluclating in a cluster takes up alot
of network resources and you might concider running a 100Mb switched
network.

SuSE and RedHat both do good NFS installs.
I suggest that you configure all your systems to start from a NFS root
mount this way you don't need to install all the software on all
systems. (I have done this several times and it works great!)

I don't know if you are familiar with parallel virtual machines (wich
beowul is) but your software need to be build against the pvm libs in
order to take advantage of the cluster. Otherwise you won't see any
advantage.

Raymond


