Jon,

if it's the original PC164, the only way to change the clockspeed is by
replacing the crystal (which should be 50.00 MHz in your case). There's a fixed
10x multiplier to get the CPU clock. The jumpers set up the division to get to
the PCI-speed.
If you tried to underclock your CPU by changing the jumpers, you were actually
overclocking the PCI-bus.
(This doesn't explain why it works at some speeds, but not at others. In fact, I
don't know if it explains anything at all ;-)
 

