I made a DOS formatted disk with LINLOAD.EXE and UDB-NONAME.GZ, but you need
to use the short filename for UDB-NONAME.GZ (UDB-NO~1.GZ).  I renamed mine
to NONAME.GZ to make it simple.
Make sure you've set up the Windows NT ARC firmware according to the MILO
faq at http://www.vesta.demon.nl/DEC/files/Alpha-FAQ/milo-5.html#ss5.1
Your boot selection should look something like:
LOADIDENTIFIER=Linux
SYSTEMPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
OSLOADER=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)\linload.exe
OSLOADPARTITION=multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
OSLOADFILENAME=\noname.gz
OSLOADOPTIONS=

I used RAWRITE to make diskettes from the GENERIC.IMG and the RAMDISK.IMG
files from the /images directory on your CD-ROM or from the FTP site.

Once ARC successfully loads the MILO you'll just need to put in the Generic
kernel image diskette and enter:
boot fd:generic.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
After that loads, you'll be prompted to put in the Ramdisk diskette.
It should then take you to the installer.

I'm just not able to install over FTP because the paths to the packages seem
to be incorrect in the installer.  So I'm d/l'ing the ISO so I can install
from CD-ROM.

Good luck,
Keith






