: first I wonder those cpml lib's what are they for and would I need to
: edit makefile's of prog's so they use that ?

cpml is for when you need maximum floating point performance. Applications
which could benefit include gs and gimp.  Yes, you need to edit the makefile
to include cpml BEFORE libm.  Unfortunately, all sort of problems can arise,
so they are most useful for very maths intensive codes where one has a good
grip on the source code (usually something one has written oneself).

