First, you CANNOT overlap partitions for Alpha Linux, as you can using
True64 UNIX.
Second, fdisk will wrap if you use the default max cylinder. use max
cylinder -1

Use the SRM install guide at the following link, Its for the DS20,10,ES40
and XP1000, but an SRM install is the same for all boxes.



http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/linux/install_guide.html

The guide is for DS10, DS20 , ES40 and XP1000, but is applicable to ALL
SRM installs. Just select the generic kernel applicable to the number of
CPU's supported, single or multi (uni or smp).

perform a "show device" at the srm prompt to list device names on your box
and substite your device names for those in the install_guide.  The
install_guide
is onle a GUIDE.

Last, make sure your graphics card is supported by linux Alpha. Especially
if
your system was sold as NT-only.

A Tested options link is at the bottom of the "install_guide" web page.

JJ

