JJ (johnj@bicnet!net) wrote:

: First, you CANNOT overlap partitions for Alpha Linux, as you can using
: True64 UNIX.

Sez who?  You can write disklabel exactly in the same manner with
Linux fdisk as you would do that for Tru64.  And if you have disk
shared between these two OSes you better make a partition 'c',
type 'unused', covering the whole disk or Tru64 will be quite unhappy.

: Second, fdisk will wrap if you use the default max cylinder. use max
: cylinder -1

This is a bug in older versions of fdisk.  Pay attention to a reported
total capacity, which is correct, and you will not go wrong.  Suggested
last cylinder on the last partition is indeed off by one.

  Michal



