gerryw@austin.rr.com wrote:

> 1. I got the alpha.iso image from one of the RedHat mirror sites and burned
> it on to a cd.
> 2. I downloaded the latest firmware update from dec/compaq (3.8 I think).

Shouldn't be necessary I think.

> 3. I tried to use the ARC facility to run linload.exe from the cd specifying
> \kernels\generic.gz as the image.
> 4. It loaded and produced the following output

Your error is thinking that the kernel is the file to point to from
linload.exe. Linload is nothing more than bootstrap code for MILO. You
should point to \milo (where milo is the milo for your architecture
(udb-noname)). It's on the iso I downloaded but I see it's compressed.
Don't know if linload.exex can gunzip it so maybe you have to do that
first (on a floppy)

> Linux Loader V1.5
> .
> .
> Setting up args at...
> Setting up memory at...
> Setting up memory at...
> Swapping to PALcode at 0x0...

> NT Firmware Monitor

> ** Opcode Reserved for DEC occurred **

> 5. I got the milo.dd image from dec/compaq and used rawrite to write it to
> floppy.

Why don't you use the image in /milo/images on the cd?

> 6. This produces a checksum error loading the floppy (I repeated step 5).
> 7. I got the latest version of linload.exe from dec/compaq and put it on a
> floppy.

Get it from the cd. It should work as I hope they tested it......

> 8. I defined a boot scenario which would read lineload.exe from the floppy
> and read the image from the cd (\kernels\generic.gz).
> 9. I got the same result as 4.

ARC boots linload.exe
(scsi(0)partition(0)rdisk(0)...........\linload.exe)
linload.exe boots MILO
(scsi(0)partition(0)rdisk(0)...........\milo)
MILO boots Linux kernel. /kernels/generic.gz is the kernel not MILO :)
(boot sr:/kernels/generic.gz root=/dev/scd0)

-- 
Daniel Tryba




