Just wanted to contribute my $.02:

In 3 days of attempting to install RH6 and the
newly available RH6.1 on an AS1000 Model 500/333
(Noritake-Primo) machine, I have finally given up.
Here are my experiences:

RH60 - There is no MILO for the Noritake-Primo so I
am looking at an SRM based install.  Right away I
know it is going to be an up hill battle, because
the RH install docs really seem to be geared toward
the ARC console.  Anyhow, I am encouraged that the
generic boot disk and install ramdisk start up
without a hitch.  I am in the RH60 installer, and
advance through an HTTP style install, having
downloaded the dist to a local linux box here and
sym-linking it to that box's apache doc root.  The
installer sees my 21041aa card, and I get to the
fdisk/diskdruid part.  Now since I am SRM, I have
to used fdisk, and not only that, fdisk my sda in
BSD disklabel mode.  So I do.  I go ahead and make
the c label covering the entire disk, as unused.  I
then go about making /, /usr, swap and /home label-
partitions as d, e, f and g.  While making these
partitions, I do experience some strange things
when setting partition sizes; at times, even though
I set the size to something like +640M, fdisk goes
haywire and sets the size to something WAY beyond
the physical disk length.  So I delete the
erroneous partition and remake it, this time
setting the partition length to an exact cylinder
number, equal to what the 640M length would be.
This works.  So I finish making the partition
table, write it, and return.  I select packages and
go forward with the install.  Everything is peachy,
including the part where I go to the Alt-F2 console
to chroot /mnt "swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx -
f3" the boot blocks onto the sda disk... UNTIL
configuring X.  I have a Cirrus Logic CL-GD5424
card, and after selecting it, the RH installer
copies over the XFree86-SVGA server.  At this time
no matter what I do, X will not configure properly.
The RH installer complains that it cannot detect
how much video ram the card has.  I quit out and
reboot, and it WORKS, but i simply cannot get and X
server to work to save my life.  No, I do not have
a Mach64 card to try, and you know I shouldn't have
to because the Cl cards are Linux's best friend.

I should note that this is the best install
experience I was able to get with RH6x Alpha.  The
RH61 install is just flat out not going to happen
with the SRM/BSD-disklabel approach.  Here's why:

RH61 - Again, the generic boot and ramdisk images
work just fine booting out of the SRM.  The problem
arises due to the nature of the RH61 installer
itself.  The RH61 installer offers no fdisk, only
diskdruid.  I know I know, I can shell and fdisk
the sda by hand, or prepare it ahead of time.  I
did this.  The installer proceeds, but craps out on
the DEC21041 ethernet card!  Can you believe it?
So I shut down and yank it, and throw an Intel
EEPro 10/100 in it.  This works, and I am able to
select packages and even install them.  When
finished copying and installing the RPMs, the RH61
installer attempts to perfom post-installtion
configuration.  PYTHON BLOWS UP.  The installer
crashes, throwing some Python dbg errors, allows
you to go interactive into the dbg if you want, but
pretty much forces a reboot.  From what I could
gather, the RH61 installer could not mount or
unmount the partitions after the RPM copy/install.
I THINK it just can't handle the BSD-disklabling,
but that is just a wild guess.  It sure seemed to
be able to handle them while copying the RPMs!

Anyhow, it seems that RH61 just will not install on
an SRM based Alpha.  I have no experience with a
MILO/ARC based install.  I even tried to "update"
my semi-successful RH60 installation, but the RH61
installer pretty much did the same thing... Python
bombed on the post-install configuration.

Anyhow, I am a bit disappointed.  You'd think
someone would test this sort of thing, but i guess
it is FREE :)

