running Redhat 6.0 with kernel 2.2.13 with address 192.168.0.110). The
rtl8139 drivers had version 1.07 (shipped with 2.2.13) and 1.08 (from the
drivers home page).

I've set up both systems for networking. The cards are connected with a
XOVER-cable and after booting I can get a ping form the PC to the Alpha and
vice versa, so the hardware (cards and cable) should be ok.

running "ifconfig eth0" I get the following outputs after trying some pings:

This is the output from the PC

eth0      Link encap:Ethernet  HWaddr 00:10:A7:01:E4:A3  
          inet addr:192.168.0.99  Bcast:192.168.0.255  Mask:255.255.255.0
          UP BROADCAST RUNNING MULTICAST  MTU:1500  Metric:1
          RX packets:26 errors:0 dropped:0 overruns:0 frame:0
          TX packets:49 errors:0 dropped:0 overruns:0 carrier:0
          collisions:0 txqueuelen:100 
          Interrupt:12 Base address:0xe800 

and this the one from the Alpha:

eth0      Link encap:Ethernet  HWaddr 00:10:A7:01:E4:A3  
          inet addr:192.168.0.110  Bcast:192.168.0.255  Mask:255.255.255.0
          UP BROADCAST RUNNING MULTICAST  MTU:1500  Metric:1
          RX packets:19 errors:7 dropped:0 overruns:5 frame:4
          TX packets:49 errors:0 dropped:0 overruns:0 carrier:0
          collisions:0 txqueuelen:100 
          Interrupt:19 Base address:0x8800 

ping on the Alpha outputs:

64 bytes from 192.168.0.99: icmp_seq=1 ttl=255 time=0.1ms
wrong data byte #8 should be 0x8 but was 0xa0

with the last byte changing for each ping message but it's always byte #8
which is different.

This looks like the Alpha has problems receiving the data from my PC.
According to the help file for the rtl8139 driver this could be a problem
