Bart (bitters98@earthlink.net) wrote:
: these lower all of my drives to only 5mb SCSI?  If so, I thought about
: just installing a second supported scsi controller, but I saw someone on
: USENET say that doing so in a 433/500a would cause "silent data
: coruption", but only in one post.

You are probably referring to my post. It is very easy to check whether
your system potentially suffers from that problem: locate your system's
serial number; if it is BELOW AB810xxxx (where AB can be NI, AY, or ZG),
your system does have a problem. It still might work, particularly if the
second adapter is NOT UltraSCSI - but it is absolutely not supported.

The problem is documented in "Digital Personal Workstations i+-Series,
a-Series, and au-Series" systems and options catalog, V3.7, published
June 19, 1998. I do not know whether you still can get that publication
from Compaq.

