Not so much on the Itanium news but...

If you look at the 733-Mhz Intel chip, it costs less than the Alpha 21264A
($4500-$5500) at 750Mhz.
The Pentium III-733 has become a champion in the workstation arena next to
the Alpha. If Intel just DOUBLES the FPU efficiency (maybe triple), the
Pentium III can outclass the Alpha chip. You can buy a
MicronPC 667-Mhz Pentium III workstation for the price of ONE Alpha 21264a
chip!!!

You can't beat the cost savings of the Intel chips or AMD clones. if
Intel/AMD improve FPU speeds on the IA-32 designs then Alpha will loose its
market share. Most business users don't use the FPU, but the engineers and
scientists will save a bundle in buying home machines with "Linux inside".





