Hello,

Some weeks ago I wrote an inquiry to this group about Java on Linux/Alpha.
At the time, I got some response from one who had JDK 1.2 up and running.
I couldn't get it to function properly on my system at the time, but things
have changed, and I thought I would post a follow up in case others out 
there are struggling with the same problems.

I'm using RH 6.0 on a 164LX with a 21164 (533MHz). I first downloaded (all 
downloads from ftp.alphalinux.org) and tried JDK 1.2, port done by Uncle 
George, port v.5. This was the latest version of the port at the time. 
It didn't run. I recently downloaded v.6 of the port, and that worked. 
But in the meantime, I had done several upgrades of my system. Of these,
here are the ones that _might_ have had an effect on the JDK:

- Kernel 2.2.13
- glibc 2.1.2
- gcc 2.91.66 (egcs 1.1.2)
- LessTif 0.89.4
- XFree86 3.3.5 (probably not important)

Now, it might have been enough to upgrade from v.5 to v.6 of the port,
but just in case others are stuck on the same problems, there you have
an (incomplete?) list of software that might help you.

As for the future of JDK on Linux/Alpha, well it doesn't look too good.
With the v.6 of the JDK 1.2 port came a notice that Uncle George had not
received a renewal of his license from Sun, and his current license 
expires this month. Blackdown seem to be a long way off getting even close
to a Alpha port. Personaly, I hope Compaq can come trough for us and put 
some force behind their porting effort of the JDK for True64 and OpenVMS 
to Linux. At this time however, no ETA or even a hint of how the work is 
progressing has been given. So if anyone at Compaq reads this, maybe they
could enlighten us as to the status of that port (that goes for the guys 
at Blackdown to by the way)?




