Peter Onion (system owner) wrote:

> > Linux supports only one GB of memory, on Alphas it can be patched to
> > support two. SMP looks fine, I'm running a couple of dual UP2000
> 
> Thanks for this.   Do you know if there is any work underway to
> increase the amount of memory that can be used ?

Rumours say that some people are working at it.
The problem is that PCI devices can only address 4GB (at least the 32
bitters)
Gather-Scatter DMA is needed.

With the kind of box you intend buying, you can probably add a few quid
and hire someone to implement Gather-Scatter DMA...
- Alex



