> /etc/X11/XF86Config
> /usr/X11R6/bin/XF86_SVGA
> /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/XF86Config@
> 
The 3.3.2.3 release of the XF86_SVGA server does not support the
'STB Nitro 64 Video' card you have in the system.  Try getting
the 3.3.5 version; it should solve your problem.  One warning:
the X font server in 3.3.5 is broken on Alpha, so don't bother
getting it, and make sure your FontPath lines in XF86Config don't
get changed during the upgrade.

One other possibility: if the original video is still in the system
as well (not sure how the XL300 is laid out), it may be finding the
DEC video first, which is TGA and requires a different server.

Hope this helps.

MarkG
