Yes, you can disable it in SRM, but Linux will use it anyway. The linux
kernel does not look at how SRM sets up the network card.

RH6.0 has been loaded on these boxes, what you want is the latest kernel.
the one in RH6.0 has problems. hit the website below



Linux Installation instructions for the SRM console are the same for All
Alpha Boxes.  Use the instructions at

http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/linux/install_guide.html

The guide is for DS10, DS20 , ES40 and XP1000, but is applicable to ALL
SRM installs. Just select the generic kernel applicable to the number of
CPU's supported, single or multi (uni or smp). in your case singe.(uni)

perform a "show device" at the srm prompt to list device names on your box
and substitute your device names for those in the install_guide.  The
install_guide
is only a GUIDE.

Last, make sure your graphics card is supported by linux Alpha. Especially
if
your system was sold as NT-only.

A Tested options link is at the bottom of the "install_guide" web page.

JJ

