Note that the -fast compilation flag can cause runtime differences
in code that is not ANSI compliant or otherwise non-portable. See
the cc man page for a description of the -fast option and the
flags that it is made up of.

Most often, when code runs as expected at the default optimization,
but not at -fast, it's a problem in the source code. What you could
try is to use -fast and then turn off some of the -fast options that
may be problematic in some code.

For example: -fast -noansi_alias

Or just use the default opt level, unles you really need to
tune your application for speed.

-Jeff

