We need more information about what system you are using.
OS, kernel version, hardware configuration...

A segmentation fault occurs when a program tries to access
memory that some other process owns.  A typical cause is 
when a program does not check whether a system call has
returned valid data before trying to use it.

Xmms and X11amp could give segmentation faults if your
sound card is configured differently than expected.  I
wouldn't guess why Licq crashes.

Hope to hear back from you,

