Actually GPL says we must make the sources available. We do.
Send me 4 blank writeable CDROMs and postage of $10 or a courier account
number to use and we will burn you a set for yourself. No charge.

What we charge money for is the support.

 First of all our Alpha Linux distribution is provided on the systems we
ship, and we include a CDROM set, with all sources.
However, we are not in the software distribution business, so we only
sell to those who explicitly wish to buy, and normally as a part of our
system bundle.
 Like Red Hat, SuSE, etc., we simply package the readily available
software. We DO add some various items and improvements, and we go to
great lengths to provide a more thoroughly tested, debugged, and secure
Linux for Alpha.

BTW, we sold the rights to the name Hard Hat Linux to another company
this year as they really wanted this brand name for a Linux for embedded
systems, and now use the name Northern Linux for our distribution.


