Chris (quattro_net@dtn.ntl.com) wrote:
: Dave Thiery wrote:
: > 
: > I just received my copy of it today and have just started going
: > through all the online documentation.  But as of yet, I haven't come
: > across anything that mentions using it along side Linux or WinNT.  How
: > do you go about setting up a system like that?  And can it be
: > installed on a system with AlphaBIOS??  Or would I have to change
: > that?
: >

: I'm just about to try installing DU on a 433a, you have to put in an
: Adaptec 2940 or another supported SCSI controller, since the _a series
: only has ide and du needs scsi. Then, just flash the bios with the _au
: version, and away we go. At least, that's the theory. Not supported in
: any way by dec, but that was targeted marketing for you.

DU does not support Adaptec yet...

: The advantage is that the _a series are currently a steal in comparison
: with the au series and the PW433 is a pretty pretty hot box, (near top
: of the list from a couple of years back) if you look at the specs.

: As for sharing drives, it's something I would avoid. Keep it simple,
: disk storage is cheap... 

SRM can only boot one OS per disk, so you can't have DU & Linux on the
same disk. If you want Linux to read the DU disk, make sure you have set
up DU using UFS rather than AdvFS. DU cannot read Linux ext2fs.

: Rgrds, Chris

