Hi,

As you probably know Compaq is going to drop its support for NT and M$ is
going to pull all its alpha based products. So, all "happy" owners of
AlphaBIOS-based NT-only boxes (like, for example, XL 233/266/300/266/433)
are going to be left without new (NT) software very soon, which is not
right. I don't care much about that, as a matter of fact, as I am running
Linux on my XL 300 box but I think that this is a good enough reason to
"ask" Compaq to address the problem: if NT support is to be dropped
something should fill the void. Why not DU? 

Actually, I am quite happy with Linux/Alpha but it would be nice to have
Tru64 (especially the $99 one ;-), *BSD, or OpenVMS (all of these require
SRM which in missing on an XL) as an option. There have been a lot of
messages from people willing to install SRM and run DU on their XLs, so I
guess the demand for the SRM/DU on XLs is quite high.

Unfortunately, my enquiry to Compaq conserning the problem generated no
reply so far but I hope that if there is a load of such enquiries from
unhappy owners of XLs running unsupported NT ;-) we may find our XLs on the
list of hardware supported by DU one day. May be not but it is worth trying
INHO.


Regards,
Andrei.



