DU will only run with SRM console, but depending on what machine you
have, you may have this in flash as well as Alphabios. If not, you can
download from one of the dec ftp sites for machines that support SRM.
For PW... machines like the 433a, which is Alpha bios only as shipped,
you can ftp SRM for the 433au variant and replace the Alphabios. XL...
series machines, OTOH, were Alphabios only, and don't have an SRM
version at all. (Correct me if there are exceptions someone) As for
install, just boot the cd and you will be led into the install program.
You have all the usual stuff to partition and label the disk, select
software subsets whatever. Couldn't be made much simpler really.

I'm just about to try installing DU on a 433a, you have to put in an
Adaptec 2940 or another supported SCSI controller, since the _a series
only has ide and du needs scsi. Then, just flash the bios with the _au
version, and away we go. At least, that's the theory. Not supported in
any way by dec, but that was targeted marketing for you.

The advantage is that the _a series are currently a steal in comparison
with the au series and the PW433 is a pretty pretty hot box, (near top
of the list from a couple of years back) if you look at the specs.

As for sharing drives, it's something I would avoid. Keep it simple,
disk storage is cheap... 

Rgrds, Chris



