: > I'm just about to try installing DU on a 433a, you have to put in an
: > Adaptec 2940 or another supported SCSI controller, since the _a series
: > only has ide and du needs scsi. 

: I don't know about PWS433a, but I have two 500a's here and both shipped
: with SRM and both have a SCSI controller and disks. Only the CD is IDE

All recent (so-called "enhanced") a-series have Qlogic 1040 SCSI controller 
on the system board (which is the same as on the au-series). Older models of 
au-series have an add-on SCSI card (KZPBA-CA), also based on Qlogic 1040
(in fact, it is simply a re-branded QLA1040).

Incidentally, do not make a mistake of buying Adaptec 2940 for your DPW -
it is not supported under Tru64, and, unlike many other unsupported cards,
it truly does not work.

