"Jasper Jans" <j.jans@cello.nl> writes:

> 1. how much performance is gained by adding 256kb cache

I tested this by compiling some Linux kernel (maybe 2.2.10) before and
after adding the cache chips. I had been running my AXPpci 33 without
the cache chips since it seemed fast enough for about everything I
did. Here are the results:

  115 minutes with no cache
  73 minutes with 20 ns cache
  66 minutes with 15 ns cache

This was on 21066 at 166 MHz with some SCSI disks and 32 MB of
RAM. So, if it starts feeling slow for some reason without cache,
adding 256 KB of it should certainly help.

